@import "./compiler.sly"
@use Project

class SlytherProject {
    A Slyther project is a folder where the slyther files live, contains the following structure:

    - main.sly: Entry point
    - .slyther: Contains the Slyther output files
    - .slyther/build
    - .slyther/build/parser.json: The JSON representation of the SlytherScript parsed from main.sly after a build
    - .slyther/artifacts: The operations of every kind as built, see #{Build::SlytherArtifactBuilder}
    - .slyther/artifacts/manifest.json: The #{Build::SlytherArtifactManifest}
    - .slyther/instances/manifest.json: The #{Check::SlytherInstanceManifest}

    .slyther/build is ignored by version control, .slyther/artifacts and .slyther/instances are committed,
    so a checkout runs the operations without building them again and a check evaluates only what changed.
}

method SlytherProject::build {
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::parse} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::buildArtifacts} method
}

method SlytherProject::parse {
    Uses #{Compiler::SlytherParser} to parse the main.sly file and writes the JSON representation to: .slyther/build/parser.json
}

method SlytherProject::buildArtifacts {
    Groups the parsed script into every #{Compiler::SlytherArtifactKind}, prints their warnings, and builds
    their operations into .slyther/artifacts with #{Build::SlytherArtifactBuilder}, returning what it did to
    every file: built, rebuilt, kept or removed
}

method SlytherProject::run {
    Runs an operation of a kind as built, given the kind, the operation and its args, which must fit the
    params of the operation, otherwise it must throw an error, as must an operation that is not built.

    A deterministic operation runs the script of each of its steps in order from the root of the project,
    with the args as positional arguments, and stops at the first that exits with a code other than 0,
    returning that code. An operation that is not deterministic returns the markdown that orchestrates it
    with every `{param}` substituted by its arg, or, when a #{Build::SlytherGenerator} is given to execute
    it, hands the markdown to it and returns its reply.
}
method SlytherProject::check {
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::parse} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::buildArtifacts} method
    Executes the #{SlytherProject::checkInstances} method
}

method SlytherProject::checkInstances {
    Checks every artifact the parsed script declares with #{Check::SlytherInstanceChecker}, given the fix and
    max options, and returns what happened to every one: pass, fail, missing, kept or fixed, with its errors
}
